script:
export const meta = {
  name: 'bonus-realtime',
  description: 'Bonus: realtime on the tenant portal (publication migration, subscription UI, RLS-isolation test)',
  phases: [{ title: 'Build' }],
}
const COMMON = `Timed build lane (hard deadline 04:20Z; keep it small). Working dir ./app. ../SPEC.md, ../DECISIONS.md. One simple command per Bash call; never npm i; never commit; NEVER db reset; DB/test commands via bash ../scripts/with-db.sh <cmd>. Dev server at :3000 (never start/kill). Edit ONLY your listed files. The existing 1192 tests must stay green.`
const S = { type: 'object', properties: { status: { type: 'string' }, files_changed: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }, checks_run: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } }, assumptions: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } }, required: ['status', 'files_changed', 'checks_run', 'assumptions'] }
const db = await agent(`${COMMON}\nTask (db-engineer): NEW migration supabase/migrations/20261026000004_realtime.sql: alter publication supabase_realtime add table public.payments, public.gateway_bills; (comment: D73 — realtime postgres_changes are filtered by RLS for the subscriber's JWT, so tenants only receive rows of their own leases; no new grants). Apply WITHOUT reset: npx supabase migration up. Verify with psql: select tablename from pg_publication_tables where pubname='supabase_realtime'. Then npx prisma db pull (expect no diff) and bash ../scripts/with-db.sh npx vitest run tests/rls/catalog.test.ts (must pass). Files: that migration only.`,
  { agentType: 'db-engineer', label: 'rt:db', phase: 'Build', schema: S })
const [ui, t] = await Promise.all([
  agent(`${COMMON}\nTask (ui-builder): files src/components/tenant/** only. In the tenant portal client component (tenant-portal.tsx — read it), after the initial load, subscribe with the browser supabase client: supabase.channel('tenant-portal').on('postgres_changes', { event: '*', schema: 'public', table: 'payments' }, refetch).on('postgres_changes', { event: '*', schema: 'public', table: 'gateway_bills' }, refetch).subscribe(); RLS limits rows to the tenant's own leases (no client-side filter needed, but you may add filter: 'lease_id=in.(...)' if simple). refetch = the existing load function (debounce ~300 ms so a webhook's bill+payment+allocations burst triggers one reload), and show a small toast 'Payment status updated' when an event arrives after the first load. Unsubscribe on unmount: supabase.removeChannel(channel) in the effect cleanup. No new packages. Done means: tsc + eslint clean.`,
    { agentType: 'ui-builder', label: 'rt:ui', phase: 'Build', schema: S }),
  agent(`${COMMON}\nTask (test-authz): tests/rls/realtime.test.ts (describe 'R42 R56 realtime respects RLS'). Using tests/helpers createFixtureOrg (tenant A on the lease, tenant B with no lease or another lease): subscribe as tenant A and as tenant B with userClient(token) to postgres_changes on public.payments (event INSERT) — remember to call client.realtime.setAuth(token) before subscribe if the helper does not; wait for status 'SUBSCRIBED' (timeout 20 s); then record a cash payment on tenant A's lease via the API as the fixture manager (api(token).post('/api/leases/<id>/payments', { amountSen: 100, method: 'cash', receivedAt: new Date().toISOString() })). Assert tenant A receives an INSERT for that payment id within 15 s and tenant B receives nothing within that window. Clean up channels in afterAll. The publication migration is being applied in parallel by db-engineer: wait until psql -tAc "select count(*) from pg_publication_tables where pubname='supabase_realtime' and tablename='payments'" prints 1 (sleep 20 between checks, up to 30). Done means: bash ../scripts/with-db.sh npx vitest run tests/rls/realtime.test.ts passes twice in a row. If realtime does not deliver to tenant A at all (environment issue), report that clearly instead of weakening the test.`,
    { agentType: 'test-authz', label: 'rt:test', phase: 'Build', schema: S }),
])
return { db, ui, tests: t }
